 ],
 "article": {
  "title": "The Eye That Notices: The Power of Observation",
  "topic": "科技创新·观察力与学习成长",
  "level": "CET-4",
  "words": 0,
  "paras": [
   "Every day we walk past hundreds of small things without really seeing them. Yet observation is one of the most powerful skills a person can build. A good observer notices what others miss: a tiny change in the sky, an unusual habit in a friend, a small flaw in a machine. Scientists, doctors and engineers all depend on this quiet ability to attract useful details from ordinary life.",
   "Why is observation so valuable? Because it is the first step of every discovery. When Newton watched an apple fall, he did not just see an apple — he saw a question. Observation leads to curiosity, and curiosity drives invention. In school, students who observe carefully often understand ideas faster, because they notice the objective facts behind abstract rules. A consistent habit of paying attention can turn a common person into a specialist.",
   "Observation can be trained like a muscle. One practical method is to pause for a minute each day and describe what is around you in detail: the color of a leaf, the order of the books on a shelf, the sound of the street. Another way is to keep a small notebook and sketch or write down three things that caught your eye. After a few weeks, you will be surprised how much your mind has sharpened.",
   "In an age of screens and speed, our attention is often scattered. Learning to observe is learning to slow down and stay conscious of the world. It makes us more sensible, more creative, and more connected to others. As the French writer once said, the real voyage of discovery lies not in seeking new landscapes, but in having new eyes. So open your eyes wide — the world is full of clues waiting for you."
  ],
  "zh": "每天我们从成百上千件小事旁边走过，却并没有真正看见它们。然而观察是一个人能够培养的最强大技能之一。好的观察者能看到别人错过的东西：天空中细微的变化、朋友不寻常的习惯、机器上的小瑕疵。科学家、医生和工程师都依赖这种安静的能力，从平凡生活中捕捉有用的细节。为什么观察如此重要？因为它是每一次发现的第一步。当牛顿看着苹果落下时，他看到的不是苹果，而是一个问题。观察引发好奇，好奇推动发明。在学校里，善于观察的学生往往更快理解知识，因为他们能看见抽象规则背后的客观事实。坚持关注细节的习惯能把普通人变成专家。观察可以像肌肉一样训练。一个实用的方法是每天暂停一分钟，详细描述周围的事物：叶子的颜色、书架上书的顺序、街道上的声音。另一种方法是随身带一个小本子，把打动你的三件事速写或记下来。几周之后，你会惊讶于自己的头脑变得多么敏锐。在这个充满屏幕和速度的时代，我们的注意力常常是分散的。学会观察就是学会慢下来，保持对世界的清醒意识。它让我们更明智、更有创造力、与他人联系更紧密。正如法国作家所说，真正的发现之旅不在于寻找新的风景，而在于拥有新的眼睛。所以，睁大你的眼睛——世界到处都是等待你的线索。",
  "hard": [
   {
    "en": "Observation is one of the most powerful skills a person can build.",
    "cn": "观察是一个人能够培养的最强大技能之一。",
